From: Noswad <64293615+TheNoswad@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gpio: max77759: ignore interrupts of unmapped GPIOs

When GPIO5/6 interrupt status is set for a GPIO that was never requested
as an interrupt, irq_find_mapping() returns 0 and handle_nested_irq(0)
dereferences a NULL descriptor, killing the max77759 interrupt thread
(seen on a USB-C disconnect with a burst of FRS signals: charger and fuel
gauge stop being serviced). Ack and skip such interrupts.
---
--- a/drivers/gpio/gpio-max77759.c	2026-10-14 14:12:13.749676023 -0500
+++ b/drivers/gpio/gpio-max77759.c	2026-10-14 14:12:13.761046088 -0500
@@ -409,6 +409,8 @@
 			break;
 
 		for_each_set_bit(offset, &pending, MAX77759_N_GPIOS) {
+			unsigned int virq;
+
 			/*
 			 * ACK interrupt by writing 1 to bit 'offset', all
 			 * others need to be written as 0. This needs to be
@@ -418,8 +420,18 @@
 			regmap_write(chip->map, MAX77759_MAXQ_REG_UIC_INT1,
 				     BIT(offset));
 
-			handle_nested_irq(irq_find_mapping(gc->irq.domain,
-							   offset));
+			/*
+			 * An interrupt can be pending for a GPIO nobody has
+			 * requested as an interrupt (no mapping yet); there is
+			 * no descriptor to hand it to then.
+			 */
+			virq = irq_find_mapping(gc->irq.domain, offset);
+			if (virq)
+				handle_nested_irq(virq);
+			else
+				dev_dbg_ratelimited(gc->parent,
+						    "spurious IRQ for GPIO%d\n",
+						    offset + 1);
 
 			handled = true;
 		}
